  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the best result so far at 0.619 acc, but only marginally (~2.8%) above the RNA-only multiprofile baseline (config_002, 0.591). Image-only performance is very weak (0.21–0.23), suggesting the image modality contributes little signal. Uncertainty: We have only tested concat fusion in the multimodal setting. It is unclear whether a weighted fusion that can learn to downweight the weak image branch would improve over the fixed equal-weight concat. Question: config_019 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while holding all other design choices (pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, multiprofile) identical to config_018, giving a clean single-variable comparison. Why best next: This is the lowest-cost, highest-information experiment available—it directly tests whether the modest image contribution can be better leveraged (or suppressed) via learned weighting, and the result will inform whether further investment in image encoders or multimodal variants is worthwhile under the limited budget."
}

